<title>TURKEY: Turkish cen bank reserves up $32 mln week to Nov 1.</title>
<headline>Turkish cen bank reserves up $32 mln week to Nov 1.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $32 million to $17.274 billion in the week to November 1.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars</p>
<p>		     November 1     October 25   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserves    17.274	  17.242	 12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserves	1.383	   1.383	  1.383</p>
<p> Total reserves    18.657	  18.625	 13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, fell by $107 million to $27.935 billion in the week ending October 18, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
